                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/22.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-19T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. Your 43, September 29, cancellation mining titles, encloses only translation
                    of Circular No. 1 of September 3, by Department of Fomento. Department desires
                    decree of August 29.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
